.TH modcompile "1" "2026-08-02" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "The Enhanced Machine Controller"
.SH NAME
modcompile \- compile HAL components, generate GMI code, manage stmakd packages

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modcompile
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR.comp ...
.br
.B modcompile gmi
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIfile\fR.gmi ...
.br
.B modcompile
\fBlist\fR | \fBrebuild\fR | \fBadd-gomod\fR \fIdir\fR | \fBrm-gomod\fR \fIname\fR
.br
.B modcompile
\fB\-\-cflags\fR | \fB\-\-ldflags\fR | \fB\-\-cmod-dir\fR | \fB\-\-include-dir\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B modcompile
builds HAL components from
.B .comp
sources, writing loadable cmod modules.  It replaces the
.B halcompile
utility of earlier LinuxCNC releases; the
.B .comp
language is largely unchanged, but the command line is not the same \- there
is no
.BR \-\-userspace ,
.BR \-\-personality ,
.B \-\-extra-compile-args
or
.BR \-\-extra-link-args ,
and only
.B .comp
files are accepted, not
.B .c
files.
.PP
It also generates client and server code from
.B .gmi
interface definitions, and manages the Go packages compiled into
.BR stmakd .

.SH OPTIONS
.SS Component compilation (.comp)
.TP
.BR \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-\-parse
Parse only; print the parsed AST as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-preprocess
Preprocess only; emit the generated C code.
.TP
.BR \-\-document
Generate man page documentation for the component.
.TP
.BR \-\-view-doc
Generate the man page and display it in the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-\-compile
Compile to a shared object in the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-install
Compile and install into the cmod directory.
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE"
Write output to
.IR FILE ,
for
.B \-\-preprocess
and
.BR \-\-document .

.SS GMI code generation (.gmi)
.TP
.BR \-\-server-c ", " \-\-server-go ", " \-\-server-meta
Generate server-side bindings.
.TP
.BR \-\-client-c ", " \-\-client-go ", " \-\-client-python ", " \-\-client-ts
Generate client bindings for the named language.  The
.B \-ws
variants generate WebSocket clients.

.SS Package registry
.TP
.B list
List the packages compiled into
.BR stmakd .
.TP
.B rebuild
Regenerate imports and rebuild
.B stmakd
from
.BR packages.conf .
.TP
.BI add-gomod " dir"
Copy a Go package into the stratuMAK tree, register it, and rebuild.
.TP
.BI rm-gomod " name"
Unregister a package, delete its source, and rebuild.

.SS Build environment queries
These print values for use by external Makefiles building components out of
tree, which is how a component written directly in C is built now that
.B .c
input is no longer accepted.
.TP
.BR \-\-cflags ", " \-\-ldflags
Compiler and linker flags for cmod components.
.TP
.BR \-\-cmod-dir ", " \-\-include-dir ", " \-\-stmak-dir
Installation directory, header directory, and stratuMAK Go module source
directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-go
Path of the Go binary used to build LinuxCNC.
.TP
.BR \-\-print-make-inc
Print a Makefile include snippet for external projects.

.SH EXAMPLES
Compile and install a component:
.PP
.RS
.nf
modcompile \-\-compile mycomp.comp
sudo modcompile \-\-install mycomp.comp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate its man page:
.PP
.RS
.nf
modcompile \-\-document \-o mycomp.9 mycomp.comp
.fi
.RE

.SH "SEE ALSO"
The HAL Component Generator chapter of the LinuxCNC documentation
describes the
.B .comp
language in full.

